               <physDesc>
                  <objectDesc>
                     <supportDesc>
                        <support>
                           <p>According to [8H6M69W4], 15783, xylograph (shing dpar), but this is, rather, a handwritten manuscript in dpe tshugs script, with many abbreviations.<lb/>A few annotations in dbu can and dbu med - the latter appear to have been written while copying the main text rather than later (e.g. fol. 3b).<lb/>In dbu can in the margin of the cover page: ba°, and the folio number 39 written as if it was the last folio of a manuscript (so dgu byon no) - it might not be related to this manuscript. <lb/>The following folios are numbered in dbu med, from 2 onward. Numbers 49 and 50 occur on the same folio. Number on the last folio: 90.<lb/>Lines per folio: 8; 6 of fol. 1b.</p>
                           <dimensions unit="cm">
                              <width>66</width>
                              <height>9</height>
                           </dimensions>
                        </support>
                        <extent>89</extent>
